abstract: >-
  A containerised, reproducible benchmark for computing the electronic ground-state
  energy of small molecules (H2, LiH, BeH2) with the Variational Quantum Eigensolver
  (VQE). The same calculation is run at several reference levels (classical exact FCI,
  exact diagonalisation of the qubit Hamiltonian, noiseless statevector, finite-shot
  sampling, and a noisy simulator or a real IBM QPU), so that mapping, ansatz,
  statistical and hardware-noise errors are quantified separately. Error-mitigation
  strategies (zero-noise extrapolation with an own ISA-safe implementation, the Mitiq
  reference implementation and the IBM Runtime built-in variant, plus measurement
  mitigation) are compared under identical conditions. Results are stored in a
  schema-versioned database that records the full software environment, produced by an
  automated, failure-tolerant pipeline, and shown in an interactive dashboard.
  (Magyarul: konténerizált, reprodukálható benchmark-rendszer kis molekulák VQE-alapú
  alapállapoti energiájának számítására, hibaenyhítési stratégiák összehasonlításával,
  szimulátoron és valódi IBM-hardveren; az eredményeket sémaverziózott adatbázisban
  tárolja és interaktív dashboardon jeleníti meg.)

keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - variational quantum eigensolver
  - quantum chemistry
  - quantum error mitigation
  - zero-noise extrapolation
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - NISQ
  - Qiskit

